values ($seed$write-proposals-that-win$seed$, 'workshop', $seed$Write proposals that win$seed$, null, 180, 'live online', 350, 25, 'draft', 'invite', 5, 20, true, 50, 50,
  $seed${"summary":"Turn a client's problem into a proposal they can say yes to.","problem":"A good proposal is not a price list. It shows the client you understood their problem, explains what they will get and what it will cost, and makes the next step easy. Many practitioners send a number in a chat message and wonder why the client goes quiet.","audience":"Practitioners who are asked for proposals or quotes and want them to read professionally.","outcomes":["Structure a proposal around the client's problem and the outcome they want.","Present deliverables, fees, timeline and responsibilities clearly.","Offer options without confusing the client.","Write terms covering payment, revisions and support.","Make the next step obvious."],"series_fit":"Brings discovery, scope and pricing from Workshops 01, 04 and 05 together into one document the client can approve."}$seed$::jsonb, $seed$get-paid-for-automation$seed$, 6, true, 'Imported from content/workshops/series as a planned workshop')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;
